        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 88-year-old female patient, admitted on 12/12/2022 due to an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia, chest X-ray showing pulmonary hyperinflation without consolidation, and blood tests revealing mild inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout the stay. Treatment consisted of supplemental oxygen therapy, inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids for hydration. The patient responded well to treatment with improvement of respiratory function. She was discharged on 13/12/2022 in stable condition. We recommend continuation of her regular COPD medication and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact us for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
